'''''Schinus weinmanniifolia''''', the '''Uruguayan pepper tree''', is a native tree of [[Uruguay]], northwest [[Argentina]], [[Paraguay]],<ref>{{GRIN | accessdate=22 July 2015}}</ref> and southern Brazil.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|title = ''Schinus lentiscifolius'' - Uruguayan pepper tree {{!}} List of species {{!}} Trees and palms {{!}} Green areas {{!}} Environmental Vectors {{!}} Environment {{!}} Barcelona City Council|url = http://w110.bcn.cat/portal/site/MediAmbient/menuitem.0d4d06202ea41e13e9c5e9c5a2ef8a0c/?vgnextoid=a848a758abcec310VgnVCM1000001947900aRCRD&vgnextchannel=3cc37037aed1a210VgnVCM10000074fea8c0RCRD&vgnextfmt=formatDetall&lang=en_GB|website = w110.bcn.cat|accessdate = 2015-07-19}}</ref> It grows to 3 to 9 metres in height with a crown width of 3 to 5 metres.<ref name=":0" />

Three varieties are recognized:<ref name = powo/>
*''Schinus weinmanniifolia'' var. ''hassleri'' {{small|(F.A.Barkley) F.A.Barkley}}
*''Schinus weinmanniifolia'' var. ''riedeliana'' {{small|Engl.}}
*''Schinus weinmanniifolia'' var. ''weinmanniifolia''

